# Session reports visibility # {#session-reports-visibility}

<div algorithm>
  To <dfn export>determine session visibility</dfn> given an [=environment settings object=] |environment| and a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].
  1. If |url| is not |session|'s [=device bound session/refresh URL=]:
    1. If the result of running [=algorithms/determine if a URL is in scope=] with |url| and |session| is false, then return "hidden".
  1. If |environment| [=environment/has storage access=], then return "visible".
  1. Return "hidden".
</div>

<!-- This is an alternative to checking for [=environment/has storage access=] above.

<div algorithm>
To <dfn>check whether credentials would be included</dfn>, given an [=environment settings object=] |environment| and a [=device bound session=] |session|:

  1. Let |url| be |environment|'s [=environment/creation URL=].
    Note: |url| can be reused from an earlier step if merged into the visibility algo.
  1. Let |request| be a new [=request=] whose [=request/URL=] is |url|, [=request/method=] is \``GET`\`, [=request/client=] is |environment|, [=request/mode=] is "`same-origin`", and [=request/credentials mode=] is "`include`".
  1. [=list/For each=] |credential| of |session|'s [=device bound session/session credentials=]:
    1. If |credential|'s [=session credential/type=] is "`cookie`", and a cookie with |credential|'s [=session credential/attributes=] would be attached to |request| (see [[RFC6265#cookie]]), then return "visible".
  1. Return "hidden".
</div>

-->

<div class="example" id="session-visibility-example">

  Issue: Consider making this a WPT instead.

  Given the following (incomplete) session definition:

  ```json
  {
    "session_identifier": "session_id",
    "refresh_url": "/refresh",
    "scope": {
      "origin": "https://example.com",
      "include_site": true,
      "scope_specification" : [
        { "type": "exclude", "domain": "sites.example.com", "path": "/" },
        { "type": "exclude", "domain": "*.example.com", "path": "/static" }
      ]
    },
    "credentials": [{
      "type": "cookie",
      "name": "auth_cookie",
      "attributes": "Domain=example.com; Path=/; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Strict"
    }]
  }
  ```

  The following table illustrates whether `session_id` is visible to various execution environments:

  <table>
    <tr>
        <th>Creation URL</th>
        <th>Storage access</th>
        <th>Visible?</th>
        <th>Reason</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/account`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>In scope of `session_id`, has storage access.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://sub.example.com/app`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Also in scope of `session_id`, by its `include_site`.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/refresh`</td>
        <td>Top-level window</td>
        <td>`true`</td>
        <td>Refresh URL bypasses scope check.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://example.com/refresh`</td>
        <td>Embedded without storage access</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>No access to 1P `example.com` storage.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://sites.example.com/a`</td>
        <td>N/A</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>URL matches the `sites.example.com/` exclusion rule.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>`https://app.example.com/static/index.html`</td>
        <td>N/A</td>
        <td>`false`</td>
        <td>URL matches the `*.example.com/static` exclusion rule.</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

</div>
